<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <img src="placeholder_jsu_logo.png" alt="JSU Logo" style="width: 150px;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 18pt;">Jacksonville State University</h2>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 5px;">Is There Something in the Drinking Water at Pete Mathieu's Coliseum?</h2>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">An interesting fact about Alabama teams of education...</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">Three of those deans have at least one degree from Jacksonville State University. What is even more...</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">Dr. <span data-field="john_b_hammett">{{ john_b_hammett }}</span>, II, is the Dean of the College of Education and Coordinator of Graduate Programs at the University of North Alabama in October 2006. She has over twenty-five years of experience in education. Immediately preceding her tenure at the College of Education and Professional Studies, Dr. <span data-field="john_b_hammett">{{ john_b_hammett }}</span> served as a department chair and faculty member. Dr. <span data-field="john_b_hammett">{{ john_b_hammett }}</span> holds a doctorate and bachelor's degrees from the University of Alabama and earned a master's degree from Jacksonville State University. Dr. <span data-field="john_b_hammett">{{ john_b_hammett }}</span> is a native of Decatur, Alabama and has a sixteen year old daughter, Allison.</p>
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 20px;">
        <div style="width: 45%; text-align: center;">
          <img src="placeholder_john_b_hammett_photo.jpg" alt="John B. Hammett" style="width: 100%;">
          <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">Dr. John B. Hammett</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 45%; text-align: center;">
          <img src="placeholder_donna_parker_photo.jpg" alt="Donna Parker" style="width: 100%;">
          <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">Dr. Donna Parker Jacobs</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 20px;">Jennifer A. Brown, Ed.D. was named Dean of the College of Education and Professional Studies at Jacksonville State University in October of 2006. Before being named at AUM, Dr. <span data-field="jenifer_a_brown">{{ jenifer_a_brown }}</span> served seven years as the associate dean of the college; and the five years prior to that she served as the department head for Foundations, Secondary and Physical Education. Dr. <span data-field="jenifer_a_brown">{{ jenifer_a_brown }}</span> earned a doctorate in Health, Physical Education, and Recreation from the University of Alabama in 1975. She earned the B.S. and M.S. degrees in health and physical education from Jacksonville State University in 1969 and 1971, respectively. Dr. <span data-field="jenifer_a_brown">{{ jenifer_a_brown }}</span> has over thirty-nine years experience as a high school and collegiate educator.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        <img src="placeholder_donna_parker_photo.jpg" alt="Donna Parker Jacobs" style="width: 100%;">
        <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">Dr. Donna Parker Jacobs</p>
      </div>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">John B. Hammett, II, PhD, was named Dean of the College of Education and Professional Studies at Jacksonville State University in October 2008. Dr. <span data-field="john_b_hammett">{{ john_b_hammett }}</span> also served as the Associate Dean of the college and Department Head for Health, Physical Education, and Recreation at JSU. Dr. <span data-field="john_b_hammett">{{ john_b_hammett }}</span> earned a doctorate in Health, Physical Education, and Recreation from the University of Southern Mississippi in 1986. He earned a B.S. and M.S. degrees in Health and Physical Education from Jacksonville State University in 1978 and 1980, respectively. Dr. <span data-field="john_b_hammett">{{ john_b_hammett }}</span> has over twenty-five years experience as an educator on the high school and college levels.</p>
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">
        <img src="placeholder_jenifer_a_brown_photo.jpg" alt="Jennifer A. Brown" style="width: 100%;">
        <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">Dr. Jennifer A. Brown</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 5px;">Ms. Sandra Fox Sudduth's Service Lauded</h2>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">Ms. <span data-field="sandra_fox_sudduth">{{ sandra_fox_sudduth }}</span> was named winner of the 2008 Cleo Education and Service Award, a University-sponsored, faculty-administered program established to honor an outstanding faculty member for his/her achievements in the area of education or service to the civic community in the Jacksonville State University area. Ms. <span data-field="sandra_fox_sudduth">{{ sandra_fox_sudduth }}</span> involvement in this community is lifelong. She moved back to Jacksonville State University after graduating from the schools. She was later placed in charge of developing the curriculum for the Anniston School System. During this time she taught adjunct.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">Ms. <span data-field="sandra_fox_sudduth">{{ sandra_fox_sudduth }}</span> was appointed to the Jacksonville City School Board. In 1990, Ms. <span data-field="sandra_fox_sudduth">{{ sandra_fox_sudduth }}</span> filled the Jacksonville City Council seat vacated by her father and has served as a member of the Jacksonville City Council for sixteen years. She also serves as Mayor Pro-Tem. In 1994, she became a full-time...</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        <img src="placeholder_sandra_fox_sudduth_photo.jpg" alt="Sandra Fox Sudduth" style="width: 100%;">
        <p style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">Ms. Sandra Fox Sudduth</p>
      </div>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">Ms. <span data-field="sandra_fox_sudduth">{{ sandra_fox_sudduth }}</span> is an instructor in the College of Education and Professional Studies. She teaches language arts in the block on campus and in Gadsden. She also serves as one of the main undergraduate EED advisors. Currently she is involved with Jacksonville Youth Council as an advisor, Big Brothers & Big Sisters Organization, Calhoun County Democratic Club, the Calhoun County Foundation Visitor Board, Farmers and Merchants Bank's Advisory Board, House of Refuge Board of Directors, Jacksonville Library Board of Trustees, and Jacksonville City Schools.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">Ms. <span data-field="sandra_fox_sudduth">{{ sandra_fox_sudduth }}</span> is truly worthy of this award and is an asset to the community, college, and the university.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom: 5px;">Dr. Larry Beard Honored</h2>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">Dr. <span data-field="larry_beard">{{ larry_beard }}</span>, associate professor of special education, in the Department of Curriculum and Instruction was recently honored by the World Head of Family Sokeship Council with a prestigious WHFSC Historical Figure Award. This award is in reference to all those instructors who have been in the arts a minimum of 40 years, who have been recognized as grandmasters in their respective arts and have made significant contributions to the martial arts block.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 1.6;">The ceremonies were held in San Antonio, Texas, where Dr. <span data-field="larry_beard">{{ larry_beard }}</span> was recognized by the World Sokeship Council for his contributions to the martial arts spanning over 40 years.</p>
    </div>
